# CSSC Licence

Copyright (c) 2026 Lilias Hatterscheidt

---

## Plain-English summary (not the licence — the terms below are)

**Part A — the toolchain** (compiler, interpreter, runtime, modules, standard
library, LSP, package manager, documentation): MIT. Do anything you want with it,
including commercially. Fork it, sell it, embed it, rename your fork. Just keep
the copyright notice.

**Part B — the IDE**: use it freely for anything, including commercially, and
modify it for your own use. What you may not do is ship a modified version, or
build another editor out of it. If you want a change in it, send it to me.

---

## 0. Components

This licence covers two separately-licensed parts of the same project.

**Part A ("the Toolchain")** — all source, binaries, and documentation in this
project **except** the files identified as Part B. This includes the compiler,
the interpreter, the runtime, the standard modules, the LSP/analyser, the
package manager and installer, and the language reference.

**Part B ("the IDE")** — the CSSC integrated development environment: its source
code, interface code, layouts, icons, themes, and other assets, as marked in the
repository.

If a file's own header names its licence, that header wins for that file. If a
file is ambiguous, it is Part A.

