## Part B — IDE Source-Available Licence

### B.1 Grant

Subject to the conditions below, you are granted a worldwide, royalty-free,
non-exclusive licence to:

a) **use and run** the IDE for any purpose, private or commercial, on any number
   of machines, with no registration and no fee;

b) **read and study** the source code without restriction;

c) **modify** the source code for your own use, including inside an organisation
   you belong to;

d) **redistribute verbatim, unmodified copies** of the IDE, provided this licence
   file and all copyright notices travel with it unchanged.

### B.2 Conditions

You may **not**, without prior written permission from the copyright holder:

1. distribute, publish, or otherwise make available to third parties a **modified**
   version of the IDE, or any work derived from its source code;

2. incorporate the IDE, or a substantial portion of its source code or assets,
   into another editor, IDE, or product;

3. distribute the IDE under a different name, or in a way that suggests it is
   your own work or an official release;

4. remove, obscure, or alter the copyright notices, licence text, or authorship
   information in the IDE.

Clause B.2.1 does not restrict changes you keep to yourself. Modify your own copy
as much as you like; the restriction begins at distribution.

### B.3 Contributions

If you send a modification, patch, or asset for inclusion in the IDE, you grant
the copyright holder a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free licence to
use, modify, relicense, and distribute it as part of the project. You keep your
own copyright in what you wrote. Nothing obliges the copyright holder to accept a
contribution.

### B.4 Name and marks

This licence grants no rights in the name "CSSC", the project's logos, or any
other mark of the copyright holder, beyond the attribution required above.

### B.5 Warranty and liability

The IDE is provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind, express or implied,
including but not limited to warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
particular purpose, and non-infringement. In no event shall the copyright holder
be liable for any claim, damages, or other liability arising from or in
connection with the IDE or its use.

### B.6 Termination

This licence terminates automatically if you breach section B.2. It is reinstated
if you cure the breach within 30 days of becoming aware of it and do not breach
again. Termination does not affect the rights of anyone who received a copy from
you in compliance with this licence.

### B.7 Severability

If any provision of Part B is held unenforceable, the remaining provisions stay
in force, and the unenforceable provision applies to the maximum extent permitted.

